# kiss_ai project ownership

## User-owned files (direct edit)

- `project.md` — the project brief (goal, topics, outputs, constraints)
- `human_design_identity.md` — project identity and design tokens
- `inputs_human/` — user documents, notes, uploads

## Centralized framework

- The shared framework lives at sibling path `../_kiss_ai/framework/`.
- Do not create a project-local `framework/` folder.
- **Do not** edit files under `_kiss_ai/framework/**` unless the user **explicitly** asks to customize the shared framework.
- If the user intentionally changes the shared framework, say so in your reply. Framework changes should be committed in the `_kiss_ai` repo, separate from this project's rebuild snapshot.

## AI-managed areas (annotation-only)

- `sources/**`, `outputs_ai/**`, `questions.md`, `.build/**`, and `change_logs/**` are AI-managed.
- Users interact with AI-managed files through `<!-- FEEDBACK: ... -->` annotation markers, not direct editing.
- The AI may leave `<!-- AI_SUGGESTION: ... -->` markers in output files for user review.
- Do not silently overwrite user annotations. Process them per `do_build.md`.
